# Shared VALUE vocabulary — ISO-4217 currency codes as language-neutral atoms.
# The atom is the lowercase alpha-3 code (the international standard identifier); human/
# multilingual names live in the translation layer. TRY (Turkish lira) -> try_ (Python keyword).
# The module is `currency_vocab`, NOT `currency`: Clausal reserves the bare name `currency`
# for its own built-in (money constructors/rounding — clausal.modules.currency), and
# _IMPORT_ALIASES rewrites every `-import_from(currency, ...)` to it unconditionally, so a
# kit module under that name is unreachable. See lint C20.
# Use: -import_from(currency_vocab, [eur, usd, ...]) + -import_module(currency_vocab);
# ref currency_vocab.eur.
#
# INTERIM. The intended end state is the built-in Decimal currency vocabulary
# (spelled-out `euro`/`sterling`/`baht` re-exported from jurisdiction modules, with
# dimension-safe arithmetic) — see todo/done/migrate-currency-to-decimal-vocabulary.md.
# That migration deleted THIS module as its first step and never took the second: the
# zero-importer sweep could not see clausify-domains, where eu/peppol_einvoicing imports
# it from six files. Restored so that domain's sealed oracle can run at all. Retiring it
# means migrating peppol's money handling, not deleting the file again.
-module(currency_vocab, [
    aed, afn, all, amd, ang, aoa, ars, aud, awg, azn,
    bam, bbd, bdt, bgn, bhd, bif, bmd, bnd, bob, brl,
    bsd, btn, bwp, byn, bzd, cad, cdf, chf, clp, cny,
    cop, crc, cup, cve, czk, djf, dkk, dop, dzd, egp,
    ern, etb, eur, fjd, fkp, gbp, gel, ghs, gip, gmd,
    gnf, gtq, gyd, hkd, hnl, htg, huf, idr, ils, inr,
    iqd, irr, isk, jmd, jod, jpy, kes, kgs, khr, kmf,
    kpw, krw, kwd, kyd, kzt, lak, lbp, lkr, lrd, lsl,
    lyd, mad, mdl, mga, mkd, mmk, mnt, mop, mru, mur,
    mvr, mwk, mxn, myr, mzn, nad, ngn, nio, nok, npr,
    nzd, omr, pab, pen, pgk, php, pkr, pln, pyg, qar,
    ron, rsd, rub, rwf, sar, sbd, scr, sdg, sek, sgd,
    shp, sle, sos, srd, ssp, stn, svc, syp, szl, thb,
    tjs, tmt, tnd, top, trl, try_, ttd, twd, tzs, uah,
    ugx, usd, uyu, uzs, ved, ves, vnd, vuv, wst, xaf,
    xcd, xof, xpf, yer, zar, zmw, zwl
])
-double_quotes(chars)
